import ir "sngl:internal/ir"

// Marks a component prop that is read while the instance is being built and
// never again: a constructor argument, a value a `var` initializer copies, a
// host property the toolkit refuses after realization.
//
// Such a prop has no setter, so a new value cannot be written into the live
// instance. Without the mark it was written into a cell nobody read, and the
// change was silently lost; with it, a render that describes a different value
// destroys the instance and builds a fresh one from the new value -- the same
// thing a changed `key=` does, and for the same reason: what the position
// describes is no longer what it holds.
//
// The cost is the instance's own state, which is why this is opt-in per prop
// rather than the default. The instance is rebuilt only when the value actually
// differs, so the prop's type has to be one every target compares alike -- the
// same requirement an effect's `on` carries. A list, a map, an option or an
// opaque `date` is not: "unchanged" is not a question the target can be asked
// about one, so the site would rebuild on every render and throw away exactly
// the state the mark exists to preserve. The mark is refused on such a type
// rather than lowered into a program whose instances live different lengths on
// each target.
//
// Only a component prop carries it -- a `var` is written by definition, and a
// declaration outside a component has no instance to rebuild.
func construct() ir.Macro
